  "description": "From the Giro d'Italia to a Saturday century with your local shop ride, the APPIA is as comfortable in a gruelling stage race as it is on a beer-themed weekend ride with friends.\nA true distillation of road cycling, the bike's size specific geometry is aggressive enough to take a corner in a criterium without sacrificing all-day comfort on long road outings. The frame's slightly sloping top tube forms a smaller, lighter and stiffer main triangle while increasing maneuverability on the bike and affording more standover height.\nThe legendary smoothness of titanium shines in the APPIA's stability on fast descents, instilling the rider with confidence through light and responsive handling. On the other side of the valley the elegant tapered head tube and seamless carbon fork provides a stiff platform for climbing.\nConnoisseurs of Pacific Northwest road cycling will recognize the geometry from the venerated Ti Cycles Hyak, and titanium aficionados will appreciate the solid construction of double butted main tubes and elegantly shaped stays. Details like a full titanium replaceable derailleur hanger, standard Di2 compatible internal construction, 68mm BSA bottom bracket and 31.6 seatpost make this the most sensible exotic bike on the market.\nWelded cable stops for external 2x shift routing\nWelded cable stops for external rear road caliper\nCompatible with standard reach rim brake calipers\nCompatible with internal electronic shift system wiring\nDi2/EPS port covers\nBright brushed finish with black decal set\nHeadbadge\nAlloy seatpost collar\n50cm frames are designed for 650c wheels only and use a standard ZS44/EC44 headset for 44mm head tubes.\n52cm-62cm frames require IS42/28.6 (45°/45° bearing) | IS52/40 (36°/45° bearing) integrated/tapered headset. Compatible models include Cane Creek 110 Series (MPN# BAA0768K) // Cane Creek Forty (MPN# BAA0783K) // Chris King DropSet 1 (MPN# F(C)2001) // FSA Orbit-C-40-ACB (MPN# 121-0514).",
